From 3443be0950515014dffc2413dc0e9152012b83a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <jelon@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:38:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 010/206] feat(shorebird): field table link info -- count and
 max_field_id match, 3 residual gaps

Implements --print_field_table_link_info_to and its _debug_info_to twin.
Now produces exactly 622 entries with max_field_id=244, matching Shorebird
on the same kernel. Not yet byte-identical; see below.

Recovered from their binaries rather than guessed:
  * FieldHasher::DuplicateAwareHash builds
      ScrubName(owner) + '.' + ScrubName(name, is_ext) + ' '
      + kind_bits + ' ' + occurrence
    Disassembly shows push_back(0x2e='.'), push_back(0x20=' '), and
    __base_10_u32 fed from 'ldur w8,[x8,#0x5f]' -- the whole kind_bits_ word,
    not individual bits. The same offset is read with >>0xb and >>0xc to test
    is_extension, which pins ConstBit at bit 0 and hence identifies bit 17.
  * id is Field::field_id(), i.e. the raw host_offset_or_field_id Smi
    ('[x+0x27]' then '>>1' in their code). Not restricted to static fields,
    which is why ids repeat across classes.
  * Their CollectAllStaticFields walks the HEAP (Heap::ResetObjectIdTable,
    UntaggedObject::VisitPointers), not class dictionaries. Iterating library
    dictionaries finds only 360 of 622; heap iteration plus hooking before the
    Drop phase reaches all 622.

Hook placement was determined empirically: at DoCompileAll's end fields are
already dropped (423 found); at its start they are not yet loaded (18412 bytes);
immediately before DropFunctions/DropFields is correct.

Three residual differences, all pointing at VM feature configuration rather than
at this code:
  1. 93 ids differ by exactly 94 in every case, so our VM has 94 more internal
     static fields occupying lower ids.
  2. 11 kind_bits differ by 131072 (bit 17, HasDeeplyImmutableTypeBit) or 65536
     (bit 16, NoSanitizeThreadBit). Bit 17 is set in kernel_loader.cc, not during
     DoCompileAll, so this is not a timing issue -- and it matches the earlier
     assembly comparison where we emit stub EnsureDeeplyImmutable and they do
     not. Shorebird appears to build with deeply-immutable disabled.
  3. Ordering within equal ids: we stable_sort after heap iteration, they
     introsort with a comparator not yet recovered.

Adds Field::kind_bits() since kind_bits_ is protected and the hash needs the
raw word.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/precompiler.cc b/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/precompiler.cc
index 33d2433d8bd..cc5768174aa 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/precompiler.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/precompiler.cc
@@ -591,6 +591,10 @@ void Precompiler::DoCompileAll() {
       FinalizeDispatchTable();
       ReplaceFunctionStaticCallEntries();
 
+      // flutter_hot_patcher: capture the field link info while every Field is
+      // still reachable -- DropFields() below removes most of them.
+      PrintFieldTableLinkInfoIfRequested(T);
+
       {
         PRECOMPILER_TIMER_SCOPE(this, Drop);
 
diff --git a/runtime/vm/object.h b/runtime/vm/object.h
index f8bc544ea62..10e6a1b5f13 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/object.h
+++ b/runtime/vm/object.h
@@ -4506,6 +4506,12 @@ class Field : public Object {
 
   bool is_static() const { return untag()->kind_bits_.Read<StaticBit>(); }
   bool is_instance() const { return !is_static(); }
+  // flutter_hot_patcher: Shorebird's FieldHasher::DuplicateAwareHash embeds the
+  // whole kind_bits_ word in the field link info, so it needs the raw value
+  // rather than individual bits.
+  uint32_t kind_bits() const {
+    return static_cast<uint32_t>(untag()->kind_bits_);
+  }
   bool is_final() const { return untag()->kind_bits_.Read<FinalBit>(); }
   bool is_const() const { return untag()->kind_bits_.Read<ConstBit>(); }
   bool is_late() const { return untag()->kind_bits_.Read<IsLateBit>(); }
